{"obsah":"<p>The last weekend of September was all about the camp, led by Marek Tryner for the men's group and Katarína Tóthová for women and girls. The weather looked terrible in the morning and the forecast was wrong, but as the morning went on things turned into a sunny day, and in the end it looks like a successful end to the year. The day before the camp Vlasta focused on individual coaching and preparing the camp and the race held the following week.</p>\n\n<p>The Czech Trial Zálesák Championship is a bit of a nod to the popular smaller Trial races of a few years ago, ridden under modified Openfree rules, and also a bit of a parody of today's Trial under the Czech Cycling Federation. Despite the rain a few enthusiasts gathered, and in the end 9 riders started in the adult category (compared to the 15 originally registered) plus a small kids' squad. The race took place at a secret forest spot that has been ridden for decades, but always only about once a year in dry conditions. In the wet it's a different league. The rules were adjusted to involve both rider performance and tactics. Simply so you had to think as well :) To everyone's surprise, the Elite 20” was won by Tobík Dolák, ahead of his guru Lukáš Valný and Pepa Neumann. In Elite 26” the win went to Vlasta Kabeláč Čiháček, ahead of Mára Tryner and Petr Jeřicha. The performance of the day came from Mára, who tried to wipe out Vlasta's lead and ended up taking a bit of a swim in the river, but it was a really interesting battle with crashes, slipping brakes and drama at the end.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>The day before the race, Vlasta, Lukáš Valný and guest rider Jířa Sehnal did an exhibition near Blansko, where unfortunately the first of them pulled his back. The exhibition was saved by Jirka Sehnal senior, who managed to bring the sound system – which was a bit further away than expected – in record time, and in the end the guys did a full 25 minutes of fooling around, which we hope the spectators enjoyed; they filled the whole space around the obstacles. Thanks for the invitation.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F10%2F20230930_094950_1.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F10%2F20230930_094950_1.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-238611\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F10%2F20230930_085751_1.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F10%2F20230930_085751_1.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-238612\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F10%2F20230930_090153_1.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F10%2F20230930_090153_1.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-238613\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F10%2F20230930_085804_1.webp?alt=media\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F2023%2F10%2F20230930_085804_1.webp?alt=media\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-238614\"/></a></figure>\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/bikeskills-web.firebasestorage.app/o/wp-content%2Fuploads%2F20